KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp26 --object-bits 12
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ element-wise addition: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
Data-parallel types ([simd.class]): element-wise addition.  No standard
library implements it yet (libstdc++ 16, libc++ 18), so the test is written to
N5008 and not checked with a compiler; it is FUTURE until a library provides
the header.  Then it is a KNOWNBUG or CORE test of CBMC's support of that
library code.
